{
    "background_story": "Edgar was a skilled craftsman who took great pride in his work as a carter, building and repairing wooden carts for the local market. He learned the trade from his father, who had learned it from his father before him. For generations, the family had been renowned for their exceptional craftsmanship and attention to detail. Edgar's carts were sought after by merchants and traders from all over the region, who valued their durability and beauty. He spent hours selecting the finest woods and carefully shaping each piece to perfection. As his reputation grew, so did his business, and soon he was able to expand his workshop and hire apprentices to help him meet the demand. Edgar's dedication to his craft and his family's legacy made him a respected figure in the community.",
